DONE (2026-08-04):

1. [x] Archived-before-push links never reach the server.
       archiveNow now queues the ids it moves that carry no server_seq, and the
       push drains that queue from the cold store (inside the `links` group, so
       chunk ordering holds). The assigned server_seq is written back to the
       ARCHIVED copy, and a cold link the server rejects under LWW is adopted
       into the archived copy rather than resurrected into the hot store. A
       one-time sweep rescues links stranded by older builds; a queue is used
       rather than scanning archived_links every sync, since the cold store is
       exactly where a big library goes to stop being read.
       Docs: docs/dev/sync.md "Archived links and the push".
       Tests: 3 cases in tests/sync/archive.spec.ts (all verified red without
       the fix) + 5 in test/archive.test.ts.

2. [x] Reading list slow under a massive seed — reviewed the trace, reproduced
       it, fixed it. Measured on 77,328 links / 75,042 week_links / 61,854
       link_tags: the page load path went ~2,860ms -> ~930ms.
       The trace's ~3s of idb request-handler self time was four whole-table
       reads per load, three of which did nothing:
         - healOrphanedEntries read the ENTIRE week_links table on every
           reconcileOpenWeeks (3x per page load) to find orphans. Only a
           tombstoned week can strand a rescuable entry, and the week_id index
           reaches those directly — now an early return in the normal case.
           ~1.3s of the 2.9s, spent finding nothing.
         - suggestLinks re-read every link moments after the page already had
           them; it now accepts the caller's array.
         - allLinks is $state.raw, not $state — it is replaced wholesale, so
           deep-proxying 77k rows for a search box was pure overhead.
       Docs: docs/dev/performance.md (with the ~900ms that remains, and why).
       Tests: 2 new cases in test/weeks.test.ts, incl. one that fails if the
       full-table scan comes back. Existing orphan guards verified to catch a
       sabotaged rewrite.

OPEN (found while measuring, NOT fixed — both need a schema change):

- suggestLinks reads the whole links table (~474ms at 77k) because the backlog
  filter (unread / un-slushed / non-resource, priority-ordered) has nothing
  indexable. A compound [priority, added_at] index would let it stop early.
- tagsByRecentUse reads all 61k link_tags (~399ms) to order ~120 tags by most
  recent use. A last_used_at column on the tag row makes it a 120-row read, but
  that is a data-model change: migration + sync.go + sync tests.

Ensure for each change:

- if data model is updated
    - There are no sync issues/regressions with the changes
    - There are adequete tests for the system to ensure no synchronization issues, and that the system works both from the UI and has unit tests
    - Features that touch frontend and backend have testing and validation for both peices
- Add Changes to the CHANGELOG.md 
    - If a version exists and does not have a release date yet, keep adding to it, if there's no versions without a release date, then bump version (e.g. `v0.1.0 -> v0.2.0`) in the version file, and add a new main heading to CHANGELOG.md for it (e.g. `v0.2.0 (unreleased)`) and add the changes under there. 
    - Add all changes under the following categories as sub-headings:
      - Features
      - Bug Fixes
      - Other
        - For things like
          - Documentation improvements
          - Refinements to existing systems that weren't bugs
          - anything else that doesn't fit in the other sections
